Article 1: The People's Court shall accept the following trademark cases:
1. Administrative cases challenging reexamination decisions or rulings made by the National Intellectual Property Administration;
2. Cases challenging other administrative acts relating to trademarks made by the National Intellectual Property Administration;
3. Cases of disputes over ownership of trademark rights;
4. Cases of disputes over infringement of trademark rights;
5. Cases of disputes over confirmation of non-infringement of trademark rights;
6. Cases of contract disputes over transfer of trademark rights;
7. Cases of contract disputes over trademark licensing;
8. Cases of contract disputes over trademark agency;
9. Cases applying for pre-litigation cessation of infringement of the exclusive right to use a registered trademark;
10. Cases applying for cessation of infringement of the exclusive right to use a registered trademark and liability for damages;
11. Cases applying for pre-litigation property preservation;
12. Cases applying for pre-litigation evidence preservation;
13. Other trademark cases.
